<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hong Xiuquan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1814">1814</a>–<a href="/years/1864">1864</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hong Xiuquan was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hakka-people">Hakka</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangdong">Guangdong</a> who, after repeatedly failing the civil service examinations, came to believe through visions and Christian tracts that he was the younger brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a>. He launched the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiping-rebellion">Taiping Rebellion</a> in 1850 and ruled the Taiping Heavenly Kingdom from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a> from 1853. He died in 1864 shortly before Qing forces took the city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hong-xiuquan.jpg" alt="Hong Xiuquan" width="320" height="363" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ford &amp; West Lith. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hong_Xiuquan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
